id: pm-64qsbl
title: Isolated release acceptance inherits npm allow-scripts through npm run
description: The published-artifact verifier passes when run with node but fails through the documented npm run wrapper with EALLOWSCRIPTS. Ambient npm_config_allow_scripts survives the temporary npmrc boundary despite --ignore-scripts. Reuse the SDK installer isolation principle in the release verifier without changing caller policy or weakening script suppression.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-18T11:45:54.086Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-18T12:04:55.212Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-18T12:03:59.072Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-18T12:03:59.072Z"
author: "harness:codex"
parent: pm-ygli86
resolution: "Construct the owned child environment without inherited allow-scripts keys, install one empty policy and prevent helper re-inheritance; preserve unrelated settings, caller state and ignore-scripts."
expected_result: The documented npm-run acceptance wrapper installs both public versions under npm and Bun despite ambient script policy and reports complete bounded lifecycle results.
actual_result: "Previously failing npm-run wrapper passes all four eleven-step registry sessions; 14 focused verifier tests, all PM-linked tests, typecheck, ESLint and duplication pass; full 9002-test suite is exact 100/100/100/100. Hosted revised-head review and validation remain required before merge."
